{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "6d09b35e-3b51-4dc5-8482-3f79f18be78e",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 1,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Sprint 1 Planning",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "86ce3d6a-9415-49f1-baf9-83851b4928b4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is the time to make some plans for this term. We will do fewer pre-assigned milestones but will instead focus on individual sprints and features for the projects.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "c7fb7a13-46d1-4035-89b5-54070d38404e",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As you think about your features, consider any feedback you collected and carefully prioritize your features. You have 9 weeks to turn your current MVP into a polished, fully working, and shipped final product! Think about your critical features and accommodate them first. Make sure your user flows work and make sense.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "042b42a8-a882-4902-b211-e33ab61b5484",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As you think ahead, you should know that this term is fast paced. You should have an alpha release ready by midterms and a beta release two weeks after that. For any consumer-facing product, you’ll want to get it into the hands of real users by week 7 or so. That last step is hard, polishing a thing and shipping it, you think you can save it for last, but you don’t want to be that group that is pulling an all-nighter before final demos. Ideally, no all-nighters should be required! 🌃",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "48c00c80-db54-4586-b686-a057ee9b8ffa",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "purple",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Tag in Master (for the end of the week)",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "fe209435-991c-4798-98c2-60216a1a7e67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At the end of the week, when you are closing out your sprint, you should tag a working version of your repos. Merge working features that you are closing into your ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "main",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " branch, make sure that each repo is in a ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "buildable",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " state (compiler checks pass, the project can be run). Then apply a tag with the name of the sprint you are closing something like ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "t2.sprint1",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ".  Naming convention can honestly be whatever you want - just as long as there is a tag.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "afe1cb8e-9933-4d40-a0e0-0e4f007a5e2d",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 3,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using git tags",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "3e3590e9-b29b-4371-a62d-119f7015ff3a",
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "props": {
        "language": "bash"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "#make sure you are in your master branch\ngit diff #make sure you are all committed and pushed\ngit tag t2.sprint1 #this will tag the current place you are at as t2.sprint1\ngit push origin --tags",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5c5daf26-cc11-4c67-81af-716e89cd6716",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "green",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
