      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🚀 Curate your Sprint",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "7e073c48-c166-44f8-b664-f6696f3ad375",
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sprint 1 is going to be a mini sprint so mostly you can put in the various assignments and any things you want to get started. ",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1cd1f37b-7b20-48b5-abea-b122609c2c88",
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "assign some tasks. Last term some teams did an AWESOME job and some did not. You know who you are, make sure you are assigning tasks and using this process.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a6d95e96-2b7b-491d-8bb7-0f41628be1a4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "pink",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Scope and Assignment",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "19790ec1-7110-40bb-920d-811b0eaf01d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remember that each issue/task should be scoped to be around 1 sit-down work session, just a couple of hours. Break up large tasks into individual smaller ones, each one should be under a few hours of work. The smaller the tasks the faster you will work (not just the appearance of speed). It is easier to take on a manageable scope issue and work through it than if the issue has multiple steps that quickly become overwhelming to think through.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dc409ca3-0407-40e7-a3ee-f664c787b1ee",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "💢 Feel free to assign each other tasks, a little aggressiveness is ok! you can interact via comments on the issues also, on a good project the board will feel like a community, people upvoting and clapping for each other, discussing the issues, or how best to implement something. EC: mention the course staff in an issue or a PR when you need help or feedback or want to say hi. We’re happy to help — and since this was a wall of text we’ll know that you happened to read it all.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e9689c80-096e-4390-b72a-c3ff697044a6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "yellow",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Start of Week Checkins",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
